# Secrets must never enter an image. The original Dockerfile did `COPY . /app`
# with no ignore file, so live API keys were baked into every published layer.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# State is a runtime volume, not an image artifact.
state/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Development noise.
.git/
.gitignore
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
tests/
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# The evaluation corpus. 4.7 MB of SYNTHETIC data used by tools/run_evaluation.py
# and the market-data tests; a running bot reads its book from the exchange, not
# from here. Excluded so the image cannot be mistaken for something that ships
# with market data baked in.
data/

# tools/ IS DELIBERATELY NOT EXCLUDED (0042).
#
# It was, and it is why this image had never built: the Dockerfile says
#
#     COPY tools/connector_check.py tools/session_tail.py ./tools/
#
# and .dockerignore removes files from the build CONTEXT before the Dockerfile
# runs, so that COPY failed with "file not found". Every deployment in this
# repo — 0038's task definition, its one-off connector task, the whole Phase D
# drill — pointed at an image nobody could produce.
#
# The obvious repair is `tools/*` plus `!tools/connector_check.py`. It is not
# used here, because re-inclusion under an excluded directory is a corner of
# Docker's matcher that this repo cannot exercise (there is no daemon in the
# sandbox), and a control whose behaviour cannot be tested is not a control.
#
# What replaces it is static and testable: the Dockerfile names every tools
# file one by one, and tests/test_fly_runtime.py refuses any COPY of a bare
# directory. No operator script reaches the image because none is named, and
# that fact is asserted rather than hoped for.
